 The agent keeps calling search_orders when the customer gives an order ID, and sometimes passes the customer's name where the ID belongs. Fix it.
+
+## Evidence
+
+Status: interface fix implemented; selection accuracy on a real model **not measured** (hand-off to adk-agent-evaluation pending).
+
+- `get_order(data)` → `get_order(order_id)`; `search_orders(value)` → `search_orders(query)`. Each docstring now says when to use the tool, names the other one, documents the ID format and gives example result dicts (13/14 bytes → 907/939 bytes).
+- `get_order` rejects values that are not order IDs (names, e-mail addresses, whitespace, path characters) with `{"status": "error", "hint": "... call search_orders ..."}` before any HTTP call. A 404 and an unavailable service also return error dicts with a hint.
+- billing_agent instruction no longer says "ALWAYS call search_orders first" (that instruction forced the reported behaviour).
